2. Free personal noncommercial use

An individual may, without paying a license fee or requesting permission, use,
copy, run, study and modify the Software for that individual's own personal
noncommercial purposes, including personal self-hosting, learning and hobby
projects. The individual may also share original or modified copies without
charge for personal noncommercial use, subject to section 3.

These permissions do not extend to business activities performed by an
individual, including freelance work, work for an employer or work for a client.

3. Conditions of permitted use and sharing

Keep this license and applicable copyright notices with copies or substantial
portions of the Software. Clearly identify modifications when sharing a modified
copy. Sharing, changing the name of the Software, or integrating it into another
project does not remove the commercial-use restriction on material covered by
this license. Do not claim the project owner's endorsement.

You may not offer broader rights to the covered Software than this license
grants. Recipients may exercise the personal noncommercial permissions directly
under this license. Separately authored material may retain its own license.

4. Commercial use requires prior written authorization

Except for rights independently available under section 5, no commercial use is
permitted without prior, express written authorization from meliwanx, the
project owner, for the rights the owner controls.

Commercial use includes, without limitation:
- using or deploying the Software for a company's or other organization's
  business operations, including internal employee tools;
- using it to perform paid professional work or work for an employer or client;
- selling, licensing, renting, bundling or integrating it into a commercial
  product, service or customer deliverable;
- operating a hosted, SaaS, API or managed service for a commercial purpose;
- paid consulting, implementation or support involving the Software.

A commercial purpose can exist even when users are not charged directly.
Personal installation, a private deployment, a fork, a renamed version, or a
version offered free of charge does not by itself qualify as noncommercial.

Request authorization through https://github.com/meliwanx/luma/issues/new or
the contact information published by the project owner. A request, an unanswered
request, or a public repository does not constitute authorization. The written
commercial agreement must specify the authorized use and any applicable scope,
fees, attribution, support, warranty and responsibility terms. Permission is
limited to that agreement; no automatic commercial license is granted here.

